IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Weapons of Mass Destruction (Prevention of Proliferation) Act 1995 (Cth) —
-- THE NOUNS, THE RULES AND THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL. Source:
-- ../registers/source-bundle/C2004A04891.txt (compilation No. 8, 6 November
-- 2018). The person who supplies or exports goods, or provides services, asks:
-- "Is what I do an offence; what is the most I can get; are my goods
-- forfeited; until when does a Minister's prohibition notice bind me?"

§ `Nouns`

-- ss 9-11.
DECLARE `Dealing` IS ONE OF
    `supplying goods to another person`
    `exporting goods that are not prohibited exports under the Customs Act`
    `providing services to another person`

-- s 6(3).
DECLARE `Who and where` IS ONE OF
    `acting in Australia or an external Territory`
    `abroad, an Australian citizen, resident or body incorporated in Australia`
    `abroad, anyone else`

-- s 14(2).
DECLARE `Section 14 notice` IS ONE OF
    `no notice`
    `a notice prohibiting the dealing`
    `a notice allowing it only on conditions`

DECLARE `WMD case` HAS
    `my dealing`                                                    IS A `Dealing`
    `who and where`                                                 IS A `Who and where`
    -- ss 9(1)(b), 10(1)(b), 11(1)(b)
    `I believe or suspect on reasonable grounds it may help a WMD program` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- ss 9(1)(c), 13
    `a permit authorises it and I keep its conditions`              IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 12
    `the Minister told me in writing there is no reason to believe or suspect so` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 14
    `the section 14 notice`                                         IS A `Section 14 notice`
    `I comply with the notice's conditions`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `I know of the contravention`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice was given on`                                       IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the notice was revoked`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day I deal`                                                IS A DATE

DECLARE `WMD position` HAS
    `I commit an offence under ss 9-11`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `I commit an offence under s 14(6)`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `maximum imprisonment in years`                                 IS A NUMBER
    `goods are forfeited`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice's last day in force`                                IS A MAYBE DATE

§ `Rules`

@ref s 6(3)
GIVEN c IS A `WMD case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act reaches me` c IF
    NOT (c's `who and where` EQUALS `abroad, anyone else`)

-- s 14(4): in force for 12 months beginning on the day given, unless revoked;
-- the period ends on the day before the corresponding day, or at the month's
-- end where there is none (changed after the independent pass).
@ref s 14(4)
GIVEN c IS A `WMD case`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the notice end for` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `the notice was given on`
    WHEN JUST d THEN JUST (IF DATE_DAY (`add months` d 12) LESS THAN DATE_DAY d THEN `add months` d 12 ELSE `the day before` (`add months` d 12))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN c IS A `WMD case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice is in force` c IF
        NOT (c's `the section 14 notice` EQUALS `no notice`)
    AND NOT (c's `the notice was revoked`)
    AND (CONSIDER c's `the notice was given on`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST d THEN
                 c's `the day I deal` AT LEAST d
             AND (CONSIDER `the notice end for` c
                  WHEN JUST e THEN c's `the day I deal` AT MOST e
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE))

-- ss 9(2), 10(2), 11(2): compliance with a s 14(2) notice's conditions.
GIVEN c IS A `WMD case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I comply with a conditional notice` c IF
        `the notice is in force` c
    AND c's `the section 14 notice` EQUALS `a notice allowing it only on conditions`
    AND c's `I comply with the notice's conditions`

-- ss 9(1), 10(1), 11(1): 8 years.
@ref ss 9-11
GIVEN c IS A `WMD case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ss 9-11 offence` c IF
        `the Act reaches me` c
    AND c's `I believe or suspect on reasonable grounds it may help a WMD program`
    AND NOT (c's `a permit authorises it and I keep its conditions`)
    AND NOT (c's `the Minister told me in writing there is no reason to believe or suspect so`)
    AND NOT (`I comply with a conditional notice` c)

-- s 14(6): knowingly contravening a notice or its conditions; 8 years.
@ref s 14(6)
GIVEN c IS A `WMD case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 14 offence` c IF
        `the Act reaches me` c
    AND `the notice is in force` c
    AND NOT (`I comply with a conditional notice` c)
    AND c's `I know of the contravention`

-- s 17(1): goods supplied or exported in contravention of the Act.
@ref s 17(1)
GIVEN c IS A `WMD case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the goods are forfeited` c IF
        NOT (c's `my dealing` EQUALS `providing services to another person`)
    AND (`the ss 9-11 offence` c OR `the s 14 offence` c)

@ref ss 6, 9-14, 17
@export default The position of a person who supplies goods, exports goods (other than prohibited exports) or provides services, under the Weapons of Mass Destruction (Prevention of Proliferation) Act 1995 (Cth): whether it is an offence (ss 9-11: believing or suspecting on reasonable grounds that it may help a WMD program, without a permit or the Minister's written all-clear under s 12, and not in compliance with a conditional s 14 notice; s 14(6): knowingly contravening a s 14 notice in force), reaching citizens, residents and Australian bodies abroad (s 6(3)); the most that can be imposed (8 years); whether goods are forfeited (s 17); and the last day a s 14 notice is in force (12 months beginning on the day given). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `WMD case`  @desc My dealing, who and where I am, my belief or suspicion, any permit, the Minister's notices, and the day
GIVETH A `WMD position`
`the WMD position for` c MEANS
    `WMD position` OF `the ss 9-11 offence` c, `the s 14 offence` c,
                      (IF `the ss 9-11 offence` c OR `the s 14 offence` c THEN 8 ELSE 0),
                      `the goods are forfeited` c, `the notice end for` c
